{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086991-undoing-bedlam-and-a-different-take-on-the-seemings","id":1086991,"title":"Undoing, Bedlam, and a different take on the Seemings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T21:00:31-07:00","id":1086991,"title":"Undoing, Bedlam, and a different take on the Seemings","content":"Disclaimer: I'm still reading through C20, so it's possible that what I write here is already addressed in the book.<br /> <br /> In reading about the Seemings and the dual dangers of Undoing and Bedlam, I find myself wondering if the Seemings could be reimagined as coping mechanisms rather than stages of life. That is, instead of Grumps being changeling who are in their final days and being worn down by Banality, what if you interpret them as changelings who have adjusted their mindset for a world where they're constantly being bombarded by Banality and thus are more resistant to Undoing than the other Seemings are? Conversely, Childlings aren't &quot;young changelings who haven't yet lost their innocence&quot; \u2014 that is, being a Childling isn't about being a new changeling who hasn't yet moved on to being a Wilder or Grump; it's about taking on a mindset that lets you immerse yourself in the things of Glamour without as much risk of Bedlam. <br /> <br /> Under this concept of Seeming, changing one's Seeming would be a deliberate choice made by a changeling in response to the environment she finds herself in: e.g., Grumps are what they are because they've been getting too close to the Undoing for their liking, and have taken on the gruff Seeming as a way of staving off the end. <br /> <br /> This is very much an incomplete thought, and full of holes both mechanically and conceptually. But I feel like there's definitely something there, a diamond in the right that just needs to be dug out and polished\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T01:14:33-07:00","id":1087046,"title":"","content":"I think that's not to far from the way they're presented in C20, to be honest? It's definitely about an approach to life, albeit one that is more common with different stages of life. I do think that maintaining the broad link - under most circumstances - to age is important. That, sure, there can be individualistic exceptions, but the default is that you progress as you age. Changeling has always been about &quot;growing up&quot; and the ways of doing that, but the inevitability that the world is going to force you into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T01:40:24-07:00","id":1087051,"title":"","content":"Still reading things as well, but I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar187_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"187\" data-vbnamecard=\"187\">beccatoria</a> here, The Seemings roughly correlate to stages in life, and while there is a thematic pressure to push changelings to go from one to the next, they're now linked to mindset instead of actual age. You can play a 30 year old Childling that has never lost touch with their innocent curiosity, or a 12 year old Grump that's already compromised to accept the state of the world. As the game notes, characters can &quot;reverse&quot; what is perceived as a one-way street with significant effort.<br /> <br /> Grumps also aren't inherently any closer to being Undone any more either, because everyone starts with the same level of Banality now. Grumps, in many ways, are actually now the best at not falling into Undoing because they have the easiest time operating around Banality without being tainted by it.<br /> <br /> This is a pretty big change from how they were presented in 2e core as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T02:45:08-07:00","id":1087069,"title":"","content":"Anecdotally, and completely not Word From On High (I mean it) I think it has something to do with all of us crusty old salt-filled grumps suddenly turning back into childlings and wilders again with the release of the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know I felt about 15 years younger working on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T02:55:50-07:00","id":1087074,"title":"","content":"Hey; I'm still firmly in the Grump Seeming \u2014 but I appreciate that in C20, that no longer means \u201cyou're an old fart who's about to keel over and die\u201d. They're now presented as an essential part of Changeling society with a vital role to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T06:21:54-07:00","id":1087647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086991-undoing-bedlam-and-a-different-take-on-the-seemings?p=1087069#post1087069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anecdotally, and completely not Word From On High (I mean it) I think it has something to do with all of us crusty old salt-filled grumps suddenly turning back into childlings and wilders again with the release of the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know I felt about 15 years younger working on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did, although now I think I'm starting to fall into Bedlam from lack of sleep staying up to read the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}